# Q40 — `Mutex[String].lock` resolves and links through a `&Mutex[String]`
# borrow parameter. Before the fix `m.lock` typechecked (typeck advertised the
# ergonomic poison-surfacing `lock` wrapper) but had NO codegen body, so any
# real call emitted an undefined `_Mutex_lock` symbol and link-failed. The
# wrapper is now a real `.rx` body in `library/std/sync/src/mutex.rx` layered on
# `lock_raw` + `is_poisoned`; `PoisonError` gained an `init` so the `Err`
# construction compiles. This pin RUNS and asserts the guarded String reads back
# correctly across the borrow boundary.
def read_locked(m: &Mutex[String]) -> String
  match m.lock
    Ok(g)  -> g.get.clone
    Err(_) -> "poisoned"
  end
end

def main
  let m = Mutex.new("hello world")
  puts "v=#{read_locked(&m)}"
end
